# Canonical identities for `git log`, `git shortlog` and `git blame`.
#
# This file only changes how names DISPLAY. It rewrites no commits, moves no
# history, and GitHub's contributor graph ignores it entirely — that graph keys
# off the author email, so merging the two accounts there means adding
# FlimtotheFlam@gmail.com to the DimitroffVodka GitHub account, not editing
# anything here.
#
# Format: <canonical name> <canonical email> [<old name>] <old email>

# ── One person, four git identities ──────────────────────────────────────────
# 709 commits went in as FlimtotheFlam, 226 + 78 as two spellings of
# Dimitroffvodka, and 25 more as FlimtotheFlam wearing the other email. Same
# author throughout; only the git config differed at the time.
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> <FlimtotheFlam@gmail.com>
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> <DimitroffVodka@gmail.com>
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> FlimtotheFlam <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com>
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> Dimitroffvodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com>

# ── Assistants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Collapses the fifteen model-name variants that accumulated in Co-Authored-By
# trailers (Opus 4.6/4.7/4.8/5, Fable 5, Sonnet 4.6, the 1M context suffixes)
# into one entry, so `git shortlog --group=trailer:co-authored-by` reports
# Claude once instead of fifteen times.
Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> <noreply@anthropic.com>

# 33 commits carry Claude as the git AUTHOR rather than as a co-author trailer,
# from sessions where the tool committed under its own identity. At the repo
# owner's direction these display as his work, so `git shortlog` reports one
# author for the project rather than two.
#
# KNOWN SIDE EFFECT, and it is unavoidable with a mailmap: 36 trailers read
# exactly `Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`, byte-identical to those author
# lines, and git cannot tell an author field from a trailer when both hold the
# same string. So co-author grouping now lists DimitroffVodka 37 times —
# self-co-authorship, which is nonsense but harmless, and confined to
# `--group=trailer:co-authored-by`. Removing the artifact would mean rewriting
# 33 commits' author fields and force-pushing, which is a far larger change
# than the display problem warrants.
DimitroffVodka <dimitroffvodka@gmail.com> Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>

# The other assistants keep their own identities — separate vendors, separate
# emails, and nothing to normalise.
